A little suggestion for NetHack3 PL8:

I want to install a NetHack-partition for many machines which will share 
the same playground over NFS. There is only one problem. Some of the machines
are DEC-stations with the MIPS-processor. This processors saves long numbers
in LSBytes - HSBytes. Exactly invers to the format of the 680xx processors.
So no other machine types can read the saved files of the DEC-stations.

A possible solution is to write save/read functions for every structure
that will be stored on disk. These functions should read/write each member
of the structure to disk. Therefore a save/read-function must exist for each 
primitive type (e.g. int and long).
The same strategies are used by TeX saving it's DVI-files.

